  Each silver thread ties heaven to the soil,
  A tender stitch that mends the fractured ground,
  Absolving sorrow, quieting our toil,
  With sweet, persistent symphony of sound.

  Until the storm begins to cease,
  And shadows drift into the dawn,
  The world awakens into peace,
  With sorrow gone.

